virtio-mem: an online memory block's unplug gives way to a changed request

A guest giving memory back as its host asks for more again waits for the
unplug under way to end before it plugs: in shards, 6 of 2,000 grows
asked for as an unplug went on took 5.1 to 5.4 s, held until the guest's
agent asked a second time (PM M466). The driver looks for a changed
request before each request to the device and before each try to take a
range (virtio_mem_send_unplug_request(), virtio_mem_fake_offline()), and
goes back to virtio_mem_run_wq() with -EAGAIN to plan again, but never
inside a try. An online memory block it unplugs whole
(virtio_mem_sbm_unplug_any_sb_online()) is taken in one
alloc_contig_range() over all of it, 128 MiB with 4 KiB pages, which
migrates every page of the range before it returns and stops early only
for a fatal signal (mm/page_alloc.c, __alloc_contig_migrate_range()),
which the driver's workqueue never has. A guest short of free memory
migrates slowly, and the changed request waits for the whole block.

Take the subblocks of an online memory block one at a time, each its own
virtio_mem_fake_offline(), which looks for a changed request first: on
one, what was taken goes back to the buddy and the main loop plans
again. What a changed request waits for is at most one subblock's
migration: a pageblock or the device's block, whichever is larger, the
unit virtio_mem_init_hotplug() already finds alloc_contig_range()
reliable at on ZONE_NORMAL and the one its fallback takes subblocks in.
A block taken whole is still unplugged in one request and removed with
its metadata, as before. Big Block Mode, which takes a big block a
section at a time (virtio_mem_bbm_offline_remove_and_unplug_bb()), is
left as it is: a device whose block is smaller than a memory block, as
shards' (2 MiB) is, is driven in Sub Block Mode.

--- a/drivers/virtio/virtio_mem.c
+++ b/drivers/virtio/virtio_mem.c
@@ -1977,17 +1977,33 @@
 					   unsigned long mb_id, int sb_id,
 					   int count)
 {
-	const unsigned long nr_pages = PFN_DOWN(vm->sbm.sb_size) * count;
+	const unsigned long sb_pages = PFN_DOWN(vm->sbm.sb_size);
+	const unsigned long nr_pages = sb_pages * count;
 	const int old_state = virtio_mem_sbm_get_mb_state(vm, mb_id);
 	unsigned long start_pfn;
-	int rc;
+	int rc, i;
 
 	start_pfn = PFN_DOWN(virtio_mem_mb_id_to_phys(mb_id) +
 			     sb_id * vm->sbm.sb_size);
 
-	rc = virtio_mem_fake_offline(vm, start_pfn, nr_pages);
-	if (rc)
-		return rc;
+	/*
+	 * Take the subblocks one at a time. alloc_contig_range() migrates
+	 * every page of its range before it returns and stops early only
+	 * for a fatal signal, which a workqueue never has: a whole memory
+	 * block taken in one call holds off a changed request until all of
+	 * it has moved. virtio_mem_fake_offline() looks for a changed config
+	 * before each subblock and returns -EAGAIN, and what was taken so far
+	 * goes back to the buddy for the main loop to plan again.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < count; i++) {
+		rc = virtio_mem_fake_offline(vm, start_pfn + i * sb_pages,
+					     sb_pages);
+		if (rc) {
+			if (i)
+				virtio_mem_fake_online(start_pfn, i * sb_pages);
+			return rc;
+		}
+	}
 
 	/* Try to unplug the allocated memory */
 	rc = virtio_mem_sbm_unplug_sb(vm, mb_id, sb_id, count);
